.TH "libnvme_set_privsep" 9 "libnvme_set_privsep" "October 2026" "libnvme API manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
libnvme_set_privsep \- Open devices through the helper
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B "void" libnvme_set_privsep
.BI "(struct libnvme_global_ctx *ctx "  ","
.BI "struct libnvme_privsep *ps "  ");"
.SH ARGUMENTS
.IP "ctx" 12
\fIstruct libnvme_global_ctx\fP object
.IP "ps" 12
Helper channel or NULL to open devices directly
.SH "DESCRIPTION"
\fBlibnvme_open\fP on \fIctx\fP returns transport handles which forward the
commands to the helper. MI endpoints are not affected. Several contexts
can share one helper channel. The channel must outlive the contexts and
their transport handles. Commands on one channel must not be issued
concurrently.
